Z||000000||mwbackus||04-16-2000||03:51 PM||||A question to those who still have the OEM floor mats for the 88 model year.  I am just looking for a description or pics(preferable) of a set of these mats.  All of the mats I have seen thus far have been aftermarket.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  I believe that the drivers side has a wear section, but I still do not know what this section is made of.<P>Thanks in advance!<BR>  <BR>Mike B.||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||04-16-2000||10:18 PM||||I have the OEM floor mats. not 88.<P>1. the carpet is an exact match.<BR>2. the ones I have don't have "wear areas" like the regular capet. They don't have any.<BR>3. the rubber backing is molded to the carpet.<BR>4. the edge stitching matches the carpet.<BR>5. they fit perfecly flat and don't extend up on the sides or front. (unless I kick them up there.) <BR>6. They cover nearly all of the flat floor area.||||reg||1
Z||000002||ChadMan||04-17-2000||08:46 AM||||The guy I bought my 88 Coupe from claimed it had factory mats, but I'm skeptical - they're light gray with the Fiero "pegasus" logo embroidered in black and maroon.<P>All the 84-87 mats I've seen have been exactly as the Ogre describes them.  Were the 88's different?  (sorry - that's probably what you're trying to find out)||||reg||1
Z||000003||mwbackus||04-17-2000||09:07 AM||||I do believe they used a different floor mat design in 88.  Ogre's description of the pre-88 mats is what I have seen before in these years.  I think in 88 there was a standard mat set, with a premium mat set also available?  I know there are several 88 trailer queens around that would have one of these two mat options.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  A picture would be great, this type of info is very important in judging the concours class at shows.<P>Mike B.||||reg||1
